\section{Abstract}
We present a unified computational engine coupling compressible fluid dynamics 
with Schlieren optical visualization to produce a physically seeded cryptographic 
architecture. Ray propagation is formulated through a constraint Hamiltonian on 
the eikonal mass shell, proving symplectic invariance under extreme density 
gradients $\|\nabla\rho\|\ge 10^4$. A fifth-order WENO solver and chaotic 
phase-mask encryption matrix bind secure bitstream generation directly to 
physical initial conditions.

