\section{Hamiltonian Ray-Tracing Formulation}
Ray trajectories follow Fermat's principle, yielding the constraint Hamiltonian
\[
H_c(\mathbf{r},\mathbf{p}) = \mathbf{p}^2 - n(\mathbf{r})^2 = 0.
\]

Hamilton's equations give the exact ray-tracing system:
\[
\frac{d\mathbf{r}}{ds} = \frac{\mathbf{p}}{n(\mathbf{r})},
\qquad
\frac{d\mathbf{p}}{ds} = -n(\mathbf{r})\nabla n(\mathbf{r}).
\]

Symplecticity is proven via Cartan's identity:
\[
\mathcal{L}_{X_{H_c}}\omega = 0,
\]
ensuring phase-space volume preservation.

