\section{Cryptographic Matrix Transformation}
Sensor-plane intensity fields $\mathbf{I}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times N}$ are 
transformed into ciphertext via
\[
\mathbf{C} = \mathbf{W}(\mathbf{I}\odot\mathbf{M})\mathbf{W}^\top + \mathbf{A},
\]
where $\mathbf{M}$ is a chaotic phase mask generated from the thermodynamic seed 
vector $\boldsymbol{\theta}(t_0)$.

Decryption requires exact recovery of $\boldsymbol{\theta}(t_0)$, making 
unauthorized reconstruction computationally infeasible.

